   "source": [
    "## La couche DAO (Data Access Object) en Java JDBC\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.content-visible when-profile=\"slides\"}\n",
    "La couche DAO (Data Access Object) permet d'abstraire complètement l'interaction avec le support de persistance, qui est généralement une base de données relationnelle. Elle centralise les opérations spécifiques liées à la persistance des données et transforme les exceptions spécifiques en exceptions applicatives gérées par l'application.\n",
    "\n",
    "Chaque entité (par exemple, une table dans la base de données) peut être associée à une classe DAO. Étant donné que la structure des opérations CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) est souvent répétitive, il est fortement recommandé de définir une interface générique et une classe générique pour les DAO.\n",
    "\n",
    "Voici les grandes lignes d'une implémentation de base pour une DAO :\n",
    ":::"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2f2492c1-bd42-4664-982d-b69387073226",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "::: {.content-visible when-profile=\"slides\"}\n",
    "- Objectif de la couche DAO\n",
    "  - Abstraire l'accès aux données pour isoler la logique métier de la persistance.\n",
    "  - Centraliser les opérations spécifiques liées à la persistance des données.\n",
    "- Associations entre entités et classes DAO\n",
    "  - Chaque entité (par exemple, une table dans la base de données) peut être associée à une classe DAO.\n",
    "  - Évite la répétition de code pour les opérations CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete).\n",
    "- Implémentation de base pour une DAO\n",
    "  1. **Interface générique** :\n",
    "     - Définir une interface avec les méthodes CRUD (create, read, update, delete).\n",
    "     - Exemple : `GenericDAO<T>`.\n",
    "  2. **Classe générique** :\n",
    "     - Implémenter cette interface dans une classe générique (par exemple, `GenericDAOImpl<T>`).\n",
    "     - Utiliser des requêtes SQL paramétrées pour les opérations.\n",
    "     - Gérer les exceptions spécifiques (transformer les exceptions SQL en exceptions applicatives).\n",
    ":::"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5ab0af49-8c28-46e6-8c1e-e74a2def9f24",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "java"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "### Interface générique DAO\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0a3cd65d",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "java"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "90ab0692",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "java"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "public interface GenericDAO<T, ID> {\n",
    "    void create(T entity) throws SQLException;\n",
    "    T read(ID id) throws SQLException;\n",
    "    void update(T entity) throws SQLException;\n",
    "    void delete(ID id) throws SQLException;\n",
    "    List<T> findAll() throws SQLException;\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c4354415",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Implantation concrète DAO\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 36,
   "id": "00ec35d8",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "java"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "// Record User pour représenter l'entité utilisateur\n",
    "public record User(Integer id, String name, String email) {}\n",
    "\n",
    "// Implémentation concrète de UserDAO\n",
    "public class UserDAO implements GenericDAO<User, Integer> {\n",
    "    private Connection connection;\n",
    "\n",
    "    public UserDAO(Connection connection) {\n",
    "        this.connection = connection;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    @Override\n",
    "    public void create(User user) throws SQLException {\n",
    "        String sql = \"INSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES (?, ?)\";\n",
    "        try (PreparedStatement pstmt = connection.prepareStatement(sql)) {\n",
    "            pstmt.setString(1, user.name());\n",
    "            pstmt.setString(2, user.email());\n",
    "            pstmt.executeUpdate();\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    @Override\n",
    "    public User read(Integer id) throws SQLException {\n",
    "        String sql = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?\";\n",
    "        try (PreparedStatement pstmt = connection.prepareStatement(sql)) {\n",
    "            pstmt.setInt(1, id);\n",
    "            try (ResultSet rs = pstmt.executeQuery()) {\n",
    "                if (rs.next()) {\n",
    "                    return new User(rs.getInt(\"id\"), rs.getString(\"name\"), rs.getString(\"email\"));\n",
    "                }\n",
    "            }\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        return null;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    @Override\n",
    "    public void update(User user) throws SQLException {\n",
    "        String sql = \"UPDATE users SET name = ?, email = ? WHERE id = ?\";\n",
    "        try (PreparedStatement pstmt = connection.prepareStatement(sql)) {\n",
    "            pstmt.setString(1, user.name());\n",
    "            pstmt.setString(2, user.email());\n",
    "            pstmt.setInt(3, user.id());\n",
    "            pstmt.executeUpdate();\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    @Override\n",
    "    public void delete(Integer id) throws SQLException {\n",
    "        String sql = \"DELETE FROM users WHERE id = ?\";\n",
    "        try (PreparedStatement pstmt = connection.prepareStatement(sql)) {\n",
    "            pstmt.setInt(1, id);\n",
    "            pstmt.executeUpdate();\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    @Override\n",
    "    public List<User> findAll() throws SQLException {\n",
    "        List<User> users = new ArrayList<>();\n",
    "        String sql = \"SELECT * FROM users\";\n",
    "        try (Statement stmt = connection.createStatement();\n",
    "             ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery(sql)) {\n",
    "            while (rs.next()) {\n",
    "                users.add(new User(rs.getInt(\"id\"), rs.getString(\"name\"), rs.getString(\"email\")));\n",
    "            }\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        return users;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
